schema: "0.3"
id: echo-of-manifestation-env-petrified-forest
type: image
service: gemini

prompt:
  text: >
    Dark fantasy concept art of the Petrified Forest — Zone 4 of the Twilight Zone. An
    ancient forest where every tree has been transmuted into black stone — obsidian-like
    trunks and branches frozen mid-growth, their surfaces glossy and reflective where they
    catch light. Leaves are suspended in mid-air, caught in the exact moment of falling,
    each one turned to thin black stone, creating a dense canopy of frozen dark shapes that
    filter moonlight into sharp geometric patterns on the stone forest floor. The ground is
    strewn with petrified fallen leaves — black stone shards that crunch underfoot. Moonlight
    filters through the stone branches in concentrated beams, creating dramatic shafts of
    pale light against the absolute blackness of the obsidian forest. The color palette is
    strictly obsidian black and amber — the only warmth comes from thin veins of amber
    mineral deposits visible in the cracked stone of some trunks, and from the cold moonlight
    that reads as slightly amber-tinted. There is absolute stillness — no wind, no movement,
    no sound. Even the shadows seem frozen. The sense is of a moment frozen forever,
    transmutation taken to its extreme — all organic life converted to mineral stillness.
    Painterly style, atmospheric lighting, dramatic contrast between moonlight shafts and
    obsidian darkness.
  negative: "bright, cheerful, cartoon, anime, clean magic, green forest, living trees, leaves blowing, wind, movement, colorful palette, blue moonlight, fantasy glowing forest, low detail, flat shading"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 1024
    aspect_ratio: "3:2"

tags: [environment, zone-4, forest, petrified, obsidian, concept-art, dark-fantasy]
